[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Generated bounded resistor model preparation

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SEM-RESISTOR-MODEL-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Prepare exact finite scalar and bounded model resistances
STATEMENT: >>>
The frontend shall retain generated resistor model-reference candidates and named instance assignments without replacing ordinary scalar recognition. Numeric and parameter-valued scalar resistance shall take precedence over same-named models. Constant R models shall contain only positive finite R and no instance overrides. Sheet models shall contain positive finite RSH and optional finite SHORT/NARROW with zero defaults, and require explicit finite positive instance L/W. The resistance shall equal RSH*(L-2*SHORT)/(W-2*NARROW), with positive finite effective dimensions and result. The native floating-point L*W*RSH sheet-selection predicate shall remain positive; underflow shall return explicit refusal rather than emulate its fallback resistance. Model values shall evaluate in the declaration model scope; geometry shall evaluate in the actual retained instance environment. Unsupported, duplicate, ambiguous, opaque, temperature, noise, AC and multiplicity terms shall refuse atomically rather than be ignored.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: ResistorModelSyntax.cs, generated resistorModelProfile, PrimitiveSyntax.cs, ResistorModelLowering.cs. Verification: ResistorModelTests tests scalar precedence, model allowlists, geometry, physical ranges, scope and actual overrides plus a reproducible FsCheck campaign. ResistorModelOracleIntegration compares original 500/600/1200-ohm R/model cards in OP, complex AC and ramp transient against ngspice, analytical dividers and both existing native providers. Parent worktree owns bridge integration; lexical preparation is not full-deck execution. Evidence: evidence/resistor-model.json and docs/resistor-model-results.md. Requirement remains Draft.
<<<
